from build import page, ROOT
content=r'''<div id="app-message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="login" class="login-panel"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVATE CLOUD OBSERVABILITY</p><h1>Your devices.<br>Your security events.</h1><p>Sign in to view metadata synchronized by your installations. This dashboard cannot execute tools, approve local actions or change local policies.</p><a class="button" href="/api/auth/github">Continue with GitHub ↗</a><p class="caption">Authentication must be configured by the operator. There is no production default account.</p><details id="dev-login" hidden><summary>Local development sign-in</summary><p class="caption">Available only on an explicitly configured loopback development server. Never use a production credential here.</p><form id="login-form"><label>Development key<input id="dev-key" type="password" required autocomplete="off" maxlength="256"></label><label>Synthetic identity<select id="dev-identity"><option value="alice">Alice (test account)</option><option value="bob">Bob (test account)</option></select></label><button>Sign in locally</button></form></details></div><div id="dashboard" hidden><div class="dashboard-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">CLOUD OBSERVABILITY</p><h1>Security overview</h1><p id="account-label"></p></div><div><div id="connection" class="status" role="status">Connecting…</div><button class="secondary" id="refresh">Refresh</button> <button class="secondary" id="logout">Sign out</button></div></div><div class="notice">Events are self-reported by linked devices. A denial is a policy outcome, not a confirmed attack. No local privileged control is exposed here.</div><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><p>Recorded events</p><strong id="metric-total">—</strong><small>Within retained history</small></div><div class="metric"><p>Allowed</p><strong id="metric-allow">—</strong><small>Gateway decision: ALLOW</small></div><div class="metric"><p>Denied</p><strong id="metric-deny">—</strong><small>Gateway decision: DENY</small></div><div class="metric"><p>Approval required</p><strong id="metric-approval">—</strong><small>Local approval only</small></div></div><nav class="dashboard-tabs" aria-label="Dashboard views"><button data-view="overview" aria-pressed="true">Overview</button><button data-view="events" aria-pressed="false">Security events</button><button data-view="devices" aria-pressed="false">Devices</button><button data-view="settings" aria-pressed="false">Account & privacy</button></nav><section id="view-overview" class="dashboard-section"><div class="section-head"><h2>Recent synchronized activity</h2><p class="caption">Latest loaded page · not a complete history chart</p></div><div class="settings-grid"><div class="settings-card"><h3>Events by day</h3><div id="timeline" class="bars"></div></div><div class="settings-card"><h3>Operation categories</h3><div id="categories" class="bars"></div></div></div><div class="notice" id="sync-summary"></div><h3>Reason codes</h3><p class="caption">Reason codes explain authorization outcomes. Unknown codes remain visible as telemetry; they are not interpreted as confirmed threats.</p><div id="reasons"></div></section><section id="view-events" class="dashboard-section" hidden><div class="toolbar"><h2>Security events</h2><label>Decision<select id="decision"><option value="">All decisions</option><option>ALLOW</option><option>DENY</option><option>REQUIRE_APPROVAL</option></select></label><label>Device on this page<select id="device-filter"><option value="">All devices</option></select></label></div><div id="event-list"></div><div class="pagination"><p id="page-status"></p><div><button id="first-page" class="secondary">Newest</button> <button id="next-page" class="secondary" disabled>Next page</button></div></div></section><section id="view-devices" class="dashboard-section" hidden><div class="section-head"><h2>Linked devices</h2><span class="caption">Last seen is historical, not an online indicator.</span></div><div id="device-list"></div><div class="settings-card"><h3>Link another installation</h3><p>Issue a one-time code, then enter it in your local Sentinel sync client. Linking does not enable local synchronization or grant tool permissions.</p><form id="pair-form" class="pair-form"><label>Device label<input id="device-name" required maxlength="50" pattern="[A-Za-z0-9 _.\-]+" placeholder="Research laptop" autocomplete="off"></label><button>Create enrollment code</button></form><div id="pair-result" hidden><p class="pairing-code" id="pair-code"></p><p id="pair-expiry" class="caption"></p><button class="secondary" id="hide-code">Hide code</button></div></div></section><section id="view-settings" class="dashboard-section" hidden><h2>Account & privacy</h2><div class="settings-grid"><div class="settings-card"><h3>Cloud synchronization</h3><p>Cloud consent alone does not enable local uploads. Your local installation must also opt in. Disabling this setting blocks ingestion for the account.</p><label class="check"><input id="sync-enabled" type="checkbox">Accept sanitized event uploads</label><button id="save-sync">Save consent</button><p id="retention" class="caption"></p></div><div class="settings-card"><h3>Delete synchronized events</h3><p>Remove this account’s cloud event records. Local audit logs remain on their originating devices. Active synchronization can upload later events.</p><button class="danger" id="delete-events">Delete cloud events</button></div><div class="settings-card"><h3>Delete account</h3><p>Permanently delete cloud account data, sessions, devices and events. Local runtime authority remains independent. Sign in again through GitHub if you choose to create a new account.</p><button class="danger" id="delete-account">Delete my account</button></div><div class="settings-card"><h3>Data boundary</h3><p>No prompts, file contents, tool responses, resource names or local paths belong in cloud event payloads. The cloud has no gateway approval or execution endpoint.</p><a href="/docs.html#privacy">Read the privacy documentation ↗</a></div></div></section></div>'''
(ROOT/'dashboard.html').write_text(page('Cloud dashboard',content).replace('<script defer src="/public.js"></script>','<script defer src="/dashboard.js"></script>'))
